  "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the water volume when $t=4$ minutes is equal to ${V}^{\u2032}(4).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\sqrt{t}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=4,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(4) & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the water volume when $t=4$ minutes is $\\frac{5}{4}$ gallons per minute.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
